{"parentUuid":"b7bb036b-c598-46ec-9e5a-516fec5af092","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a8a448561dbacf07c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014565yD68oTZs82V4TqvNGA","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"codelion OpenEvolve GitHub 2026 release production cut discovery\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Releases · algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/codelion/openevolve/releases\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/codelion/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"OpenEvolve: An Open Source Implementation of Google DeepMind's AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/blog/codelion/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"openevolve · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/openevolve/\"},{\"title\":\"Automated Discovery of High-Performance GPU Kernels with OpenEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/blog/codelion/openevolve-gpu-kernel-discovery\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - celerycelery/openevolve: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/celerycelery/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"Issues · codelion/openevolve\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/codelion/openevolve/issues\"},{\"title\":\"@codelion on Hugging Face: \\\"🧬 Hey everyone! Just released **OpenEvolve** - an open-source implementation…\\\"\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/posts/codelion/735622263233891\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - SuperCodeTool/OpenEvolving: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/SuperCodeTool/OpenEvolving\"},{\"title\":\"https://github.com/codelion/openevolve\",\"url\":\"https://www.threads.com/@shravonix_com/post/DKIHvhNtisl\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about OpenEvolve and its 2026 releases:\n\n## OpenEvolve 2026 Release Information\n\nOpenEvolve version 0.2.27 was released on March 18, 2026, which appears to be the latest production release in 2026. Earlier 2026 releases include version 0.2.26 released on January 28, 2026, and version 0.2.25 released on December 23, 2025.\n\n## About OpenEvolve\n\nOpenEvolve is an open-source implementation of the AlphaEvolve system, and it is primarily focused on novel scientific discovery and optimization programs.\n\n## Recent Achievements\n\nOne significant discovery mentioned in the search results is the automated discovery of GPU kernels that substantially outperform expert-engineered baselines, with OpenEvolve successfully optimizing Metal kernels for transformer attention on Apple Silicon.\n\nThe project is maintained on GitHub at codelion/openevolve (also referenced as algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve), and continues to receive regular updates and community contributions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"08f0be09-d970-4164-a1ab-54fb6a52e218","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:30.823Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b7bb036b-c598-46ec-9e5a-516fec5af092","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ddb2f0b7-0444-4bb0-b4b4-53d584093545","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a8a448561dbacf07c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012Wf49Ts93coEHRyyqdx4V8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AlphaEvolve DeepMind 2025 2026 follow-up paper combinatorial optimization\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: A Gemini-powered coding agent for designing advanced algorithms — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/DeepMind.com/Blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/AlphaEvolve.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[2506.13131] AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.13131\"},{\"title\":\"What GenAI Taught Us About the Future of Global Optimization | ORMS Today\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/do/10.1287/orms.2026.01.01/full/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google-deepmind/alphaevolve_results · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaevolve_results\"},{\"title\":\"AI as a research partner: Advancing theoretical computer science with AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://research.google/blog/ai-as-a-research-partner-advancing-theoretical-computer-science-with-alphaevolve/\"},{\"title\":\"Global Optimization for Combinatorial Geometry Problems Revisited in the Era of LLMs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2601.05943v1\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve Tackles Kissing Problem & More - IEEE Spectrum\",\"url\":\"https://spectrum.ieee.org/deepmind-alphaevolve\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaEvolve\"},{\"title\":\"OpenEvolve: An Open Source Implementation of Google DeepMind's AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/blog/codelion/openevolve\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about AlphaEvolve and follow-up work related to combinatorial optimization:\n\n## AlphaEvolve Overview\n\nAlphaEvolve is an evolutionary coding agent for designing advanced algorithms based on large language models such as Gemini, developed by Google DeepMind and unveiled in May 2025. AlphaEvolve is an evolutionary coding agent powered by large language models for general-purpose algorithm discovery and optimization that pairs the creative problem-solving capabilities of Gemini models with automated evaluators that verify answers, and uses an evolutionary framework to improve upon the most promising ideas.\n\n## Follow-up Research on Combinatorial Optimization\n\nThere is a notable 2026 follow-up study addressing AlphaEvolve's combinatorial optimization results. Recent progress in LLM-driven algorithm discovery, exemplified by DeepMind's AlphaEvolve, has produced new best-known solutions for a range of hard geometric and combinatorial problems, raising a natural question about the extent to which modern off-the-shelf global optimization solvers can match such results when problems are formulated directly as nonlinear optimization problems (NLPs), with researchers revisiting a subset of problems from the AlphaEvolve benchmark suite. Without any solver modifications, both solvers reproduce, and in several cases improve upon, the best solutions previously reported in the literature, including the recent LLM-driven discoveries.\n\nA follow-up to the AlphaEvolve study provided relevant literature to the LLM and prompted it to provide mathematical insights, which could be used to add valid inequalities to the generated optimization model, strengthening the dual bound.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ae808abc-b9a5-4f7c-a96f-b310bbdeb5b8","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:33.060Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ddb2f0b7-0444-4bb0-b4b4-53d584093545","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"71bceb6c-0b1d-41c8-9010-ecd8da203b8c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a8a448561dbacf07c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XZeCHdhn3EF67PKhHU8ZL9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"FunSearch DeepMind 2025 2026 follow up extension SAT optimization\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FunSearch: Making new discoveries in mathematical sciences using Large Language Models — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/funsearch-making-new-discoveries-in-mathematical-sciences-using-large-language-models/\"},{\"title\":\"This is the author’s version of the work accepted in Nature.\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/DeepMind.com/Blog/funsearch-making-new-discoveries-in-mathematical-sciences-using-large-language-models/Mathematical-discoveries-from-program-search-with-large-language-models.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Can We Use AI to Discover Better Algorithms? | Richard Cornelius Suwandi\",\"url\":\"https://richardcsuwandi.github.io/blog/2025/llm-algorithm-discovery/\"},{\"title\":\"FunSearch.pdf - Computer Science\",\"url\":\"https://cs.nyu.edu/~davise/papers/FunSearch.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google-deepmind/funsearch · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/funsearch\"},{\"title\":\"Generative Modeling for Mathematical Discovery\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2503.11061v1\"},{\"title\":\"i i “main” — 2025/3/18 — 1:26 — page 701 — #1 i i i i i i\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2503.11061\"},{\"title\":\"Research — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/research/\"},{\"title\":\"An AI system to help scientists write expert-level empirical software\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.06503v1\"},{\"title\":\"FunSearch — How Deepmind uses LLM to solve a Mathematic problem that has never been solved | by Fisher Lok | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://fisherlok.medium.com/funsearch-how-deepmind-uses-llm-to-solve-a-mathematic-problem-that-has-never-been-solved-17a9f705f771\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding FunSearch and related developments:\n\n## FunSearch Overview\n\nFunSearch is a method to search for new solutions in mathematics and computer science published in Nature. FunSearch works by pairing a pre-trained LLM with an automated \"evaluator\", which guards against hallucinations and incorrect ideas.\n\n## Original Applications\n\nFunSearch discovered new solutions for the cap set problem, a longstanding open problem in mathematics, and was used to discover more effective algorithms for the \"bin-packing\" problem.\n\n## 2025 Extension: AlphaEvolve\n\nA significant follow-up development occurred in 2025. In May 2025, Google DeepMind announced AlphaEvolve, an evolutionary coding agent powered by large language models for general-purpose algorithm discovery and optimization. \n\nUnlike FunSearch, which focuses on discovering single functions, AlphaEvolve is designed to evolve entire codebases and develop much more intricate algorithms. Google DeepMind is planning an Early Access Program for selected academic users and exploring possibilities to make AlphaEvolve more broadly available.\n\n## Note on SAT Optimization\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about FunSearch or these systems being applied to SAT (Boolean satisfiability) optimization problems. The documented applications focus on mathematical problems like the cap set problem and bin packing, though the results suggest these methods could potentially extend to other domains.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ecaddeb2-f0a1-4120-8bab-a78c17e74a43","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:36.382Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"71bceb6c-0b1d-41c8-9010-ecd8da203b8c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"16376cee-fb27-4b0d-af49-14d9eea951a0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a8a448561dbacf07c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vr4kHwUdVt4UAujgkh9sre","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"LLM driven cut generation MIP CP-SAT 2025 2026 evolutionary search\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Large Language Model-driven Large Neighborhood Search for Large-Scale MILP Problems | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=teUg2pMrF0\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ai4co/awesome-fm4co: Recent research papers about Foundation Models for Combinatorial Optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ai4co/awesome-fm4co\"},{\"title\":\"QuantaAlpha: An Evolutionary Framework for LLM-Driven Alpha Mining\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2602.07085v1\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co: Awesome machine learning for combinatorial optimization papers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co\"},{\"title\":\"A survey on large language models driven meta-optimizers for automated intelligent optimization | Artificial Intelligence Review | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10462-025-11470-w\"},{\"title\":\"A Systematic Survey on Large Language Models for Evolutionary Optimization: From Modeling to Solving\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.08269v1\"},{\"title\":\"A Systematic Survey on Large Language Models for Algorithm Design | ACM Computing Surveys\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/full/10.1145/3787585\"},{\"title\":\"SolSearch: An LLM-Driven Framework for Efficient SAT-Solving Code Generation (ICSE 2025 - New Ideas and Emerging Results (NIER)) - ICSE 2025\",\"url\":\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2025/icse-2025-nier/9/SolSearch-An-LLM-Driven-Framework-for-Efficient-SAT-Solving-Code-Generation\"},{\"title\":\"Infeasibility Aware Large Language Models for Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2604.01455v1\"},{\"title\":\"The State Of LLMs 2025: Progress, Progress, and Predictions\",\"url\":\"https://magazine.sebastianraschka.com/p/state-of-llms-2025\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the key findings related to your query about LLM-driven cut generation, MIP, CP-SAT, and evolutionary search:\n\n## Major Recent Work\n\nThe most directly relevant recent work is LLM-LNS, an LLM-driven Large Neighborhood Search framework for large-scale MILP problems published as an ICML 2025 spotlight paper. The approach features a dual-layer self-evolving LLM agent where the inner layer evolves heuristic strategies to ensure convergence, while the outer layer evolves evolutionary prompt strategies to maintain diversity.\n\nThe LLM-LNS framework surpasses manually designed LNS algorithms, ML-based LNS methods, and large-scale solvers such as Gurobi and SCIP, as well as advanced ML-based MILP optimization frameworks like GNN&GBDT and Light-MILPopt.\n\n## Broader Research Trends\n\nThe integration of LLMs with evolutionary computation has emerged as a transformative frontier, with LLMs transcending manual coding constraints by generating executable optimization algorithms from textual specifications.\n\nCurrent systematic coverage includes four categories: LLMs for Modeling, LLMs as Optimizers, Low-level LLMs for Optimization Algorithms, and High-level LLMs for Optimization Algorithms.\n\nRecent 2025-2026 papers on LLM-driven optimization include work on generalizable heuristic generation through LLMs with meta-optimization and various evolutionary approaches for combinatorial optimization.\n\nThe search results show a vibrant research area with significant activity in 2025-2026, though I didn't find papers specifically focused on CP-SAT cut generation in these results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"dacb2a8f-9fcc-4a1a-a138-fee409847fd9","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:37.397Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"16376cee-fb27-4b0d-af49-14d9eea951a0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
