{"parentUuid":"421d89d5-30c5-4d6d-ba8c-741f538da7c0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a8a448561dbacf07c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bcu8Pg3iqQWDtnDbyhYPXm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OpenEvolve TSP example combinatorial optimization Anthropic Claude 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Releases · algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve/releases\"},{\"title\":\"CodeEvolve: an open-source evolutionary framework for algorithmic discovery and optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.14150v4\"},{\"title\":\"algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Skills Marketplace - Browse & Download Claude Code Skills Free\",\"url\":\"https://claudeskills.info/skills/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills: A curated list of awesome Claude Skills, resources, and tools for customizing Claude AI workflows · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills\"},{\"title\":\"Sign in - Claude\",\"url\":\"https://claude.ai/login\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2511.23473v1\"},{\"title\":\"Anthropic\",\"url\":\"https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/AI-resistant-technical-evaluations\"},{\"title\":\"OpenEvolve: An Open Source Implementation of Google DeepMind's AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/blog/codelion/openevolve\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about OpenEvolve, TSP, and combinatorial optimization in 2026:\n\n## OpenEvolve and Combinatorial Optimization\n\nOpenEvolve includes large codebase support through LLM changes and a TSP example using this approach. OpenEvolve is an open-source evolutionary coding framework that uses Large Language Models (LLMs) to automatically discover and optimize algorithms, designed as a research-grade tool for autonomous code optimization.\n\n## Framework Architecture\n\nOpenEvolve is an evolutionary coding agent that transforms LLMs into autonomous code optimizers by maintaining populations of program variants and evolving them over generations using quality-diversity algorithms. Google DeepMind's AlphaEvolve is an evolutionary coding agent that uses Large Language Models to optimize code through an iterative process, which has been used to make breakthroughs in mathematical algorithms and optimize critical computing infrastructure.\n\n## Claude Integration\n\nFor circle packing problems, Gemini-Flash-2.0 + Claude-Sonnet-3.7 worked best in OpenEvolve's LLM ensemble. The secondary model can be configured as anthropic/claude-3.7-sonnet, indicating Anthropic's Claude models are integrated into OpenEvolve's framework for evolutionary optimization tasks.\n\nThe search results confirm that OpenEvolve does include TSP (Traveling Salesman Problem) examples for combinatorial optimization, supporting multiple LLM backends including Anthropic's Claude models.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3b95eaa7-334d-4fde-90fb-9dfbf5d4a301","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:06.372Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"421d89d5-30c5-4d6d-ba8c-741f538da7c0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b70a17e1-7387-4851-821b-4ebd5b207ac2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a8a448561dbacf07c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XUWFY7NVCLDQwW5pLqwZ7w","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DeepSeek V3 API pricing 2026 per million tokens input output\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Models & Pricing | DeepSeek API Docs\",\"url\":\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing\"},{\"title\":\"Deepseek API Pricing (Updated 2026) – All Models & Token Costs\",\"url\":\"https://pricepertoken.com/pricing-page/provider/deepseek\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek AI Pricing - Free Chat & Affordable API | 2025 Guide\",\"url\":\"https://deepseek.ai/pricing\"},{\"title\":\"pricing-details-usd | DeepSeek API Docs\",\"url\":\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing-details-usd\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V3 API Pricing 2026 - Costs, Performance & Providers\",\"url\":\"https://pricepertoken.com/pricing-page/model/deepseek-deepseek-chat\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V3 Pricing Calculator\",\"url\":\"https://neuraltalk.ai/calculators/deepseek-v3\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V3.2 - API Pricing & Benchmarks | OpenRouter\",\"url\":\"https://openrouter.ai/deepseek/deepseek-v3.2\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek Pricing 2026: API Cost, Free Tier & Plans Guide\",\"url\":\"https://felloai.com/deepseek-pricing/\"},{\"title\":\"Deepseek V3 by DeepSeek — Pricing, Specs & API Access | Inworld\",\"url\":\"https://inworld.ai/models/deepinfra-deepseek-v3\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek V3 Pricing: API Costs, Hosting Options, and Real-World Scenarios | DeployBase\",\"url\":\"https://deploybase.ai/articles/deepseek-v3-pricing\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's the current DeepSeek V3 API pricing for 2026:\n\nDeepSeek V3 pricing starts at $0.27 per million input tokens and $1.10 per million output tokens through the official API as of March 2026.\n\nIt's worth noting that pricing varies depending on where you access the API:\n- **Official DeepSeek API**: The lowest rates mentioned above\n- **Third-party providers**: Third-party hosts (Together, Fireworks) add 2-9x markup\n- **OpenRouter**: Charges per token, typically $0.30-0.50 per million, roughly 2-3.5x official rates\n\nThis is significantly cheaper than GPT-4 Turbo and Claude Opus while matching or beating both on reasoning benchmarks.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"662a6998-cd7e-402a-995d-c552a8ee5197","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:16.238Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b70a17e1-7387-4851-821b-4ebd5b207ac2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"662a6998-cd7e-402a-995d-c552a8ee5197","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a8a448561dbacf07c","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019KSoc3Hmfva9GUGEJ9G3wX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"数据齐了，给最终结论。\n\n---\n\n## OpenEvolve 半年进展\n- **最新 release**: v0.2.27（2026-03-18），半年内 5 个迭代版本（v0.2.23 起每月一发）。pip 安装即用，仍标 \"research grade\"。\n- **production-ready 等级**: **late beta**——dacite 配置简化、env-var API key、CUDA 内存管理、确定性 seed、event-based early stopping 已落地；但官方仍写 \"research grade\"，未自称 production。\n- **LLM backend**: 任何 OpenAI-compatible API。Gemini 2.5 Pro/Flash、Claude（v0.2.26 修了 Anthropic 参数 bug，circle packing 案例直接用 Gemini-Flash-2.0 + Claude-3.7-Sonnet 双模型 ensemble 拿 SOTA）、Ollama/vLLM/LM Studio 本地、OptiLLM 路由。**直接支持 Claude**。\n- **离散优化契合度**: v0.2.26 加了 **TSP example**（large-codebase 模式），ARC-AGI-2 + SLDBench 也进 examples。**仍无 SAT/CP/MIP/LBBD 案例**——TSP 是最近的对照点。\n\n## AlphaEvolve 学术后续\n- 正式 paper: **arXiv 2506.13131**（2025-06）+ DeepMind 已公开 `google-deepmind/alphaevolve_results` 仓库。\n- **2026 反例**: 一篇 follow-up 把 AlphaEvolve benchmark 用 off-the-shelf NLP solver 直接打——多个问题 solver 不改也能复现/超过 LLM 结果。意思：**LLM 优化在 well-formulated 数学题上不一定打赢成熟求解器**，但加 LLM 提示再做 valid inequality 加固 dual bound 是另一条路（这条跟 LBBD cut 关系最近）。\n- OSS 复现: **OpenEvolve** 是主流复现，另有 **CodeEvolve**(arXiv 2510.14150)、**ThetaEvolve**(arXiv 2511.23473)。\n\n## 类似工具半年进展\n- **FunSearch**: 没有显式 v2，被 AlphaEvolve 取代（DeepMind 自己定位\"FunSearch evolves single function, AlphaEvolve evolves codebase\"）。\n- **LLM-LNS** (ICML 2025 spotlight): 双层 self-evolving LLM 做 MILP large neighborhood search，**实测打过 Gurobi/SCIP + GNN&GBDT 基线**——这是离 LBBD 最近的方法学。\n- **SolSearch** (ICSE 2025 NIER): LLM 直接生成 SAT solver code。\n- 综述: arXiv 2509.08269（LLM4EvoOpt）+ ACM Computing Surveys 3787585（LLM4Algo Design）。\n\n## 项目契合度修正\n- **R10 \"1 周 PoC\" 现在是: 2-3 天**。pip install + 改 evaluator + 复用 TSP example 模板。Claude backend 已到位不用自己 wrap。\n- **API 成本**:\n  - 原 R2 估 $25 / 500 iter（Gemini Flash 老价）。当前 Gemini 2.5 Flash $0.30/$2.50 per M tok ≈ **$10-15 / 500 iter**（便宜了 40%）。\n  - Claude Opus 4.7 $5/$25 per M tok：500 iter 约 **$80-150**（贵 4-6 倍，但 prompt cache 90% off 后 ≈ $30-50）。\n  - **DeepSeek V3** $0.27/$1.10 per M tok：500 iter ≈ **$5**——最便宜，circle packing/TSP 已验证小模型 + 强模型 ensemble 工作良好，DeepSeek 当 primary 完全可行。\n- **AI Safety Contract 对齐 still 有效**: OpenEvolve 默认是离线生成 → evaluator 打分 → diff，**evaluator 是用户写的 Python**。把 evaluator 限定为\"只读 candidate ordering / hint 输出\"、不写 checkpoint，contract 100% 兼容。\n\n## verdict\n- **P2 #14 现在是: 立即可做（demoted PoC → quick spike）**。半年成熟度足够，不再是\"自己 fork 改\"，是\"pip install + 写 evaluator\"。\n- **推荐**: **OpenEvolve v0.2.27 + DeepSeek V3 主 + Claude Sonnet 4.6 副 ensemble**，复用 TSP example 骨架做 cut/hint discovery evaluator。预算 $20-50 / 一轮 500 iter spike。Go/no-go gate: spike 出的 hint 在 24h shadow run 里能否把 binding subproblem 平均求解时间降 ≥ 5%——降不到 5% 就 KILL（避免 micro-optimization 螺旋）。\n\nSources:\n- [OpenEvolve GitHub](https://github.com/codelion/openevolve)\n- [OpenEvolve Releases](https://github.com/codelion/openevolve/releases)\n- [HuggingFace OpenEvolve blog](https://huggingface.co/blog/codelion/openevolve)\n- [AlphaEvolve DeepMind blog](https://deepmind.google/blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/)\n- [AlphaEvolve arXiv 2506.13131](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.13131)\n- [Global Optimization revisited (NLP solver vs AlphaEvolve)](https://arxiv.org/html/2601.05943v1)\n- [LLM-LNS for MILP (ICML 2025)](https://openreview.net/forum?id=teUg2pMrF0)\n- [LLM4EvoOpt survey arXiv 2509.08269](https://arxiv.org/html/2509.08269v1)\n- [SolSearch ICSE 2025 NIER](https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2025/icse-2025-nier/9/SolSearch-An-LLM-Driven-Framework-for-Efficient-SAT-Solving-Code-Generation)\n- [Claude API pricing 2026](https://www.aipricing.guru/anthropic-pricing/)\n- [Gemini API pricing 2026](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing)\n- [DeepSeek V3 API pricing 2026](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3682,"cache_read_input_tokens":35855,"output_tokens":2318,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3682},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2318,"cache_read_input_tokens":35855,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3682,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3682,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Cassfn3FzWMRHEunZUjb9","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"0c3762db-ad0d-4339-adad-da7de30fabc6","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:00.629Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
